<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Color</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>color                                    list your colors
color &lt;type&gt; &lt;foreground&gt; &lt;background&gt;   set one color
color &lt;type&gt;                             set that one back to the game's color
color reset                              set all of them back
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>color room_title cpg bn
</pre>
<p>Valhalla lets you choose the colors of what you see. A foreground color is 
c and a letter, or cp and a letter for the bright one; a background color 
is b and a letter:
</p>
<pre>n  black     r  red      g  green    y  yellow
b  blue      m  magenta  c  cyan     w  white
</pre>
<p>So cpg is bright green, cr red, bn a black background. The example makes 
room titles bright green on black.
</p><p>The types you can color:
</p>
<pre>default, death, exit, group, prompt, respond, time, weather, log, wiz, 
xpgain, score, mail, clan, spells, whisper,
room_title, room_descr, obj_title, obj_descr, npc_title, npc_descr, 
pc_title, pc_descr, immort_title, immort_descr,
hit_me, hit_opponent, hit_other, miss_me, miss_opponent, miss_other, 
nodam_me, nodam_opponent, nodam_other, shield_me, shield_opponent, 
shield_other,
say_self, say_other, shout_self, shout_other, social_self, 
social_other, tell_self, tell_other,
who, who_name, who_guild, who_title, who_inv
</pre>
<p>Typing color alone shows how each is set now.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Prompt</a>
</pre>




</div>